Help for GEOIP:

GEOIP blocks connections from chosen countries (2-letter ISO codes,
e.g. RU) or networks (Autonomous System Numbers, e.g. 7018). Each
connecting user's IP is looked up in the MaxMind GeoLite2 databases;
a match places a K-Line on that IP.

Users who are logged in to services, IRC operators and services'
own clients are never matched. New users are checked about two
seconds after they connect, so SASL and burst logins are seen.
IPs or masks on the exemption list are never matched either.

Durations: a number of seconds, or a number followed by one of
s, m, h, d, w, y (e.g. 10m, 1h, 7d). Use 0 or "perm" for a
permanent K-Line. Entries without their own duration use the
network default (24 hours unless changed in the configuration).

Syntax: GEOIP ADD BADCOUNTRY <CC> [duration] <reason>
        GEOIP ADD BADASN <ASN> [duration] <reason>
        GEOIP MOD BADCOUNTRY|BADASN <target> DURATION <duration|default>
        GEOIP MOD BADCOUNTRY|BADASN <target> REASON <reason>
        GEOIP DEL BADCOUNTRY <CC>
        GEOIP DEL BADASN <ASN>
        GEOIP LIST
        GEOIP EXEMPT ADD <ip|mask> <reason>
        GEOIP EXEMPT DEL <ip|mask>
        GEOIP EXEMPT LIST
        GEOIP SCAN [EXEC]

GEOIP MOD changes an entry's duration or reason; "default" makes
it follow the network default again. It only affects new K-Lines.

Each new K-Line is reported to the services log (e.g. a log
channel that includes "info"); during a flood, at most 5 per
10 seconds are shown, followed by a count of the rest.

Adding a country or ASN only affects new connections. To check
users who are already online, run GEOIP SCAN: on its own it only
reports who would be K-Lined; GEOIP SCAN EXEC K-Lines them.

Examples:
    /msg &nick& GEOIP ADD BADCOUNTRY XX 7d Abuse from this country
    /msg &nick& GEOIP ADD BADASN AS64500 Abusive hosting provider
    /msg &nick& GEOIP EXEMPT ADD 192.0.2.* Trusted webchat gateway
    /msg &nick& GEOIP MOD BADCOUNTRY XX DURATION 30d
    /msg &nick& GEOIP SCAN
    /msg &nick& GEOIP SCAN EXEC
    /msg &nick& GEOIP DEL BADCOUNTRY XX
